@flexiarg commitment/reaffirm-goal-doubt-vehicle
@title Reaffirm the Goal, Doubt the Vehicle
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-9VD0Tc turn-Y67SoE; first proposed for: An operator mid-review of an annotation round (R1) about a company's role in a larger mission.
@why [relationship-coherence/held-uncertainty]

! conclusion: State the continued commitment to the goal explicitly and in the same breath scope the doubt strictly to the vehicle, keeping both on the table.

  + IF:
    The operator still endorses the long-term goal but has lost confidence that the current vehicle (company, project, instrument) will deliver it.

  + HOWEVER:
    Raising the doubt outright invites either abandoning the vehicle prematurely or sounding like the goal itself is in question.

  + THEN:
    State the continued commitment to the goal explicitly and in the same breath scope the doubt strictly to the vehicle, keeping both on the table.

  + BECAUSE:
    The move holds two incompatible-seeming positions open together (commitment to ends, doubt about means) rather than collapsing to one; held-uncertainty names the general discipline, this names the goal/vehicle split.
